{
  "_comment": [
    "Roles offered by the CBAT outcome questionnaire (/survey/:token), grouped by service.",
    "Data-only and imported directly by the frontend, the same way categories.json is.",
    "",
    "PROVENANCE DIFFERS BY GROUP, and that matters when reading the answers back.",
    "The Royal Air Force group reuses the exact `key` values from cbatBatteries.json, which",
    "were transcribed from real OASC 'Aptitude Scores' sheets. Those keys are authoritative,",
    "and because they match, a questionnaire answer joins straight onto the battery the",
    "Aptitude Report already scores that role against - no mapping table needed.",
    "",
    "Every other group is written from published recruitment role names rather than from a",
    "score sheet we hold. They are believed accurate but are NOT verified the way the RAF",
    "ones are, so treat a non-RAF answer as the respondent's own description of their role.",
    "This is exactly why `other` exists and why the form keeps its free-text box: if the",
    "'other' option starts collecting real traffic, that is the signal that a service's",
    "role names need correcting here rather than evidence that respondents are confused.",
    "",
    "Keys are permanent once shipped - a stored SurveyResponse.role refers to one - so",
    "rename a `label` freely but never a `key`."
  ],

  "otherKey": "other",

